CORE
shapes.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ volatile through an alias: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ more qualified is more specialized: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ through an alias as well: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.type.cv]/1, [temp.alias]/2: an alias template specialization
of a volatile type is volatile (on bin53 only const survived the alias).
[temp.deduct.type]/8, [temp.deduct.partial]: `const volatile T' requires
both qualifiers and is more specialized than `const T' or `volatile T',
also when written through an alias template.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept the program.
